WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:19.325
A few minutes later, the kids were in the main room facing the adults.

2
00:00:19.326 --> 00:00:23.175
Venna glared at the stowaways. "This is outrageous!

3
00:00:23.176 --> 00:00:26.212
The expedition is supposed to be top secret."

4
00:00:26.213 --> 00:00:30.768
"Does that mean we have to turn back?" Gliss sounded almost hopeful.

5
00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:36.637
"If so, the furies will have to rest for a few days before departing again," Tok warned.

6
00:00:36.638 --> 00:00:42.501
"Impossible." Venna frowned. "The king and queen won't appreciate any delay.

7
00:00:42.502 --> 00:00:47.875
Besides, there's no need to turn back. These kids can zap themselves home.

8
00:00:47.876 --> 00:00:51.510
We aren't close enough to the Cave yet to interfere with their magic."

9
00:00:51.511 --> 00:00:58.960
"No zapping," Tok said. "The furies will sense that level of magic. They'll get distracted and crash."

10
00:00:58.961 --> 00:01:07.311
Zann gulped. Tok had warned them earlier about not using any major magic during the journey. Now he understood why.

11
00:01:07.312 --> 00:01:11.906
"Perda and Darb will have to come with us then." Teplo glanced at Tok.

12
00:01:11.907 --> 00:01:14.430
"Is it safe to summon a message moth?

13
00:01:14.431 --> 00:01:17.200
We should let their parents know they're with us."

14
00:01:17.201 --> 00:01:21.825
"Yes, that minor sort of magic should be okay," Tok said.

15
00:01:21.826 --> 00:01:28.516
"We can't use magic?" Perda whispered to Zann. "It's like Morb is back again!"

16
00:01:28.517 --> 00:01:37.556
"Don't say that." Zann shuddered. "Let's explore the rest of the ship."

17
00:01:37.557 --> 00:01:40.422
"Prepare for landing!" Tok called out.

18
00:01:40.423 --> 00:01:46.874
Zann peered out the window. It was the next morning, and the sky was streaked with the remnants of sunrise.

19
00:01:46.875 --> 00:01:51.417
Below lay a vast desert littered with rocks and blowing red sand.

20
00:01:51.418 --> 00:01:56.949
Swirls of energy spurted out of a jagged opening, which looked like a mouth full of teeth.

21
00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:00.899
"The Cave of the Unknown," Zann whispered.

22
00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:08.816
After hearing his parents talk about the place all his life, he was really here!

23
00:02:08.817 --> 00:02:15.246
As the group exited the aircraft, Tok warned everyone not to use magic in or around the Cave.

24
00:02:15.247 --> 00:02:18.632
"We've got something to help you. I'll fetch it now."

25
00:02:18.633 --> 00:02:24.094
"This place is amazing!" Perda said, staring at the cave opening in front of them.

26
00:02:24.095 --> 00:02:28.210
"Maybe we'll see some of the famous relics we learned about in school.

27
00:02:28.211 --> 00:02:33.029
Like the Mask of Zanta, or even the Horn of the Otherworld."

28
00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:37.704
Gliss shivered. "I'm not going in there. What if we get lost?

29
00:02:37.705 --> 00:02:41.287
We won't be able to use magic to find our way out."

30
00:02:41.288 --> 00:02:45.898
Teplo heard her. "Don't worry, that's what cave crawlers are for."

31
00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:48.610
"Cave crawlers?" Perda echoed.

32
00:02:48.611 --> 00:02:53.744
"Yes. Here they are." Tok had just returned, carrying a wire cage.

33
00:02:53.745 --> 00:03:00.957
Inside were a dozen large rodents with pale fur, long tails, and huge, glowing eyes.

34
00:03:00.958 --> 00:03:05.673
"Yuck!" Gliss said. "They look like swamp rats!"

35
00:03:05.674 --> 00:03:13.027
"You'll each get one," Tok said. "They're native to this area, so they know how to avoid the Cave's energy bursts.

36
00:03:13.028 --> 00:03:17.865
The glowworms they eat give their bodies a natural glow you can use as a light.

37
00:03:17.866 --> 00:03:23.023
And no matter how lost you get, your crawler can find the way out of the Cave."

38
00:03:23.024 --> 00:03:28.567
He set down the cage. Zing lunged toward it, shooting flames.

39
00:03:28.568 --> 00:03:33.528
"Zing, no!" said Zann, grabbing the dragon. He looked at Tok.

40
00:03:33.529 --> 00:03:38.749
"Sorry, I guess he thinks they're food. I hope he didn't scare them."

41
00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:43.362
"Once your crawler bonds to you, nothing will scare it off," Tok said.

42
00:03:43.363 --> 00:03:47.271
"Be careful not to let Zing actually catch one though."

43
00:03:47.272 --> 00:03:51.375
Tok placed a crawler on Zann's shoulder and muttered a quick spell.

44
00:03:51.376 --> 00:03:56.287
Even that little bit of magic made the energy storms intensify.

45
00:03:56.288 --> 00:04:00.544
"There," said Tok. "This crawler is bonded to you now."

46
00:04:00.545 --> 00:04:07.047
The crawler dug its claws into Zann's shoulder and chirped nervously at Zing, who was watching it intently.

47
00:04:07.048 --> 00:04:11.215
Meanwhile Tok bonded crawlers to each of the other members of the group.

48
00:04:11.216 --> 00:04:17.938
"All right, everyone," Venna called out. "We'll begin by locating and cataloging each relic.

49
00:04:17.939 --> 00:04:24.632
I've drawn a diagram of the Cave based on the ancient texts and divided it into several sections."

50
00:04:24.633 --> 00:04:28.109
Venna continued to talk, but Zann stopped listening.

51
00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:36.828
"How can she make something as exciting as exploring the Cave of the Unknown sound so boring?" he whispered to his friends.

52
00:04:36.829 --> 00:04:40.261
He wondered what his parents' last journey to the Cave had been like.

53
00:04:40.262 --> 00:04:45.623
He stuck his hand into his pocket and touched the stone. To his surprise, it felt warm.

54
00:04:45.624 --> 00:04:47.765
"Weird," he muttered.

55
00:04:47.766 --> 00:04:49.823
"What?" Perda asked.

56
00:04:49.824 --> 00:04:58.693
"Nothing." Zann shivered as he took a step toward the gaping cave mouth. "Let's go in."

57
00:04:58.694 --> 00:05:01.694
The kids spent the next hour exploring the Cave.

58
00:05:01.695 --> 00:05:04.808
Sounds echoed off the cold rock walls.

59
00:05:04.809 --> 00:05:08.715
Tiny, strange creatures scurried through the shadows.

60
00:05:08.716 --> 00:05:13.166
"Oops!" Perda blurted out as they crossed a large, shadowy chamber.

61
00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:15.600
"What's wrong?" Zann asked.

62
00:05:15.601 --> 00:05:22.746
"I tripped over a rock or something." Perda leaned down. "Actually, it looks like another relic."

63
00:05:22.747 --> 00:05:28.931
Gliss gasped. "Not just any relic. I think it's the Horn of the Otherworld!"

64
00:05:28.932 --> 00:05:35.839
"Careful!" Darb said. "Don't touch—whoa!" He skidded on some loose stones and fell.

65
00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:39.162
"Darb! Are you okay?" Gliss cried.

66
00:05:39.163 --> 00:05:41.808
"Sure. I just skinned my knee."

67
00:05:41.809 --> 00:05:47.503
Gliss hurried over. "Let me see." She rubbed her fingers to do a Healing spell.

68
00:05:47.504 --> 00:05:50.096
"No magic!" Zann shouted.

69
00:05:50.097 --> 00:05:56.960
It was too late. Energy crackled from Gliss' fingertips, and the Horn lit up. Zann felt the air sizzle.

70
00:05:56.961 --> 00:05:59.419
Zap!

71
00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:03.345
"Ow!" he exclaimed, landing hard in a different tunnel.

72
00:06:03.346 --> 00:06:06.208
A second later his friends landed beside him.

73
00:06:06.209 --> 00:06:08.799
"What happened?" Gliss cried.

74
00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:14.801
"You used magic," Perda said. "The Horn must have zapped us away!"

75
00:06:14.802 --> 00:06:17.788
"Where are we?" Gliss sounded panicky.

76
00:06:17.789 --> 00:06:22.382
"Don't worry," Darb said. "Our crawlers can find the way out."

77
00:06:22.383 --> 00:06:25.895
Zann cocked his head. "Maybe they won't have to.

78
00:06:25.896 --> 00:06:29.742
I hear someone talking. We must have landed near the entrance."

79
00:06:29.743 --> 00:06:32.038
He hurried in the direction of the voice.

80
00:06:32.039 --> 00:06:34.197
It was coming from the next chamber.

81
00:06:34.198 --> 00:06:37.919
"Hello," Zann called as he entered the chamber. "We—"

82
00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:41.440
Zann took one look at the speaker and gasped.

83
00:06:41.441 --> 00:06:45.603
It was Morb!
